# Hardware coverage beyond the base lists: real PCs and laptops of many makers, and virtual machines.
# Sizes are the .deb Size from the trixie index (the squashfs grows by about that much).

# Intel iGPU firmware, Skylake onwards (e.g. skl_dmc_ver1_27.bin = display power states, skl_guc/huc). It is only a
# *Recommends* of firmware-misc-nonfree, and apt-recommends is off, so it was NOT in the image. 6.4 MB.
firmware-intel-graphics

# Battery/power profiles in the Plasma power applet: powerdevil only *Recommends* it. 56 KB.
power-profiles-daemon

# Hardware video decode on Intel gen9+ (Skylake): VA-API driver "iHD". mesa-va-drivers does not cover Intel. 3.4 MB.
intel-media-va-driver

# --- 0.1.1 general subset (docs/hardware.md has the full matrix and what waits for 0.1.2) ---

# Broadcom Wi-Fi (brcmfmac, many Dell/Apple/Lenovo laptops). Not firmware-b43: old BCM43xx cards need non-free drivers. 5.4 MB.
firmware-brcm80211

# Audio on Intel laptops from Tiger Lake onwards (Sound Open Firmware); without it: "Dummy Output". 1.4 MB.
firmware-sof-signed
# UCM profiles that SOF/AVS/Chromebook-class audio needs to route jacks and mics. 92 KB.
alsa-ucm-conf

# 2-in-1 laptops: screen auto-rotation and ambient light sensor. 36 KB.
iio-sensor-proxy

# Virtual machines. qemu-guest-agent: QEMU/KVM/virt-manager/Proxmox; spice-vdagent: clipboard and
# window auto-resize in SPICE; open-vm-tools: VMware shutdown/time sync (no -desktop yet, it pulls gtkmm). 0.56 + 0.06 + 0.70 MB.
qemu-guest-agent
spice-vdagent
open-vm-tools

# --- firmware kept by hand because --firmware-chroot is OFF (sizes: .deb, MB) ---
# Mediatek Wi-Fi/Bluetooth (MT7921/22/25, common in recent AMD laptops). 19.6
firmware-mediatek
# Nvidia GPUs with the open nouveau driver (Maxwell onwards need it for acceleration). 39.5
firmware-nvidia-graphics
# Small ones that real laptops use: Intel misc (cameras, sensors) 1.9, old Intel audio 0.8, Cirrus audio amps 0.3,
# cheap USB Wi-Fi dongles (ath9k_htc, carl9170) ~0.
firmware-intel-misc
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-cirrus
firmware-ath9k-htc
firmware-carl9170
# NOT kept (the saving): firmware-marvell-prestera, firmware-nvidia-tesla-535-gsp, qlogic/netronome/bnx2x/netxen/cavium
# (server NICs), siano/ivtv (TV tuners), libertas/ipw2x00/zd1211/b43 (old, rare Wi-Fi).
